  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-07T22:30:50.309Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "----Problem----\n\nSo this used to be a feature on the website but as avatar data was pushed to the local client the ability to \"Unshow\" avatars are now gone.\n\nNot having this means that avatar hider in events such as the \"community meetup\" would be useless. As you need to show hosts avatars at any distance and if the whole instance is shown then you have to spend 5 minutes hiding everyone.\n\nThe feature would just set all shown avatars to use safety settings. Similar to what it did on the website originally.\n\nIf this is actually possible right now please make it easier to do because I assume I wouldn't be the only user encountering this problem.\n\n----Amendment----\n\nSo after inspection you can do this by wiping all avatar cache data. This however includes all users (Hidden or shown), It would be nice to let users choose between deleting shown or hidden avatars in game. \n\n----Current Solution----\n\nIf you need to delete either all shown or all hidden avatars follow these steps:\n\n1) Go into the file directory: %AppData%\\..\\LocalLow\\VRChat\\VRChat\\LocalPlayerModerations\n\n2) You may see 1 or multiple files in here (These are users that have used on your device) Select the the user id of the account you are using (You can find this if you use the Vrchat website and look at the URL in the profile section)\n\n3) Open a text editor such as notepad and you should see a list of user id's and numbers next to them such as  \"005\" and \"004\n\n4) If you want to delete all entries with show avatar delete all Id's that have the number \"005\" and if you want to delete all entries of hide avatar delete the Id's that have \"004\" next to them\n\n5) Save the file and play Vrchat.\n\n----Final Comment-----\n\nUsers on pc can easily do this task through a script or manually deleting these entries but for the majority of the platform (Quest users) doing this task would be a difficult and most users wouldn't be able to delete these two entries independently. Most people hide troublesome individuals and never want to see those individuals' avatars again. However the current system wipes all the avatar data and means that these individuals are unhidden/ Unshown.\n\nI think this is a harmless addition to the game and while it is niche it would help users with massive amounts of users shown such as myself.",
